                    </tbody>
                </tgroup>
            </table>
        </section>
        <section id="page-breaks">
            <title>Breaks</title>
            <table id="page-breaks__table">
                <tgroup cols="5">
                    <thead conkeyref="ref-headers/head-properties"/>
                    <tbody>
                        <row>
                            <entry><codeph>break-before</codeph></entry>
                            <entry>Forces or avoids a break before a block, a row or a row group. <codeph>page</codeph>, <codeph>always</codeph> and <codeph>all</codeph> start a new page. <codeph>left</codeph> and <codeph>verso</codeph> start the next left page, and <codeph>right</codeph> and <codeph>recto</codeph> the next right page, with a blank page when needed. <codeph>avoid</codeph> and <codeph>avoid-page</codeph> move the break to an earlier place. <codeph>column</codeph> breaks only in columns.</entry>
                            <entry><codeph>auto</codeph>, <codeph>avoid</codeph>, <codeph>avoid-page</codeph>, <codeph>page</codeph>, <codeph>always</codeph>, <codeph>all</codeph>, <codeph>left</codeph>, <codeph>right</codeph>, <codeph>recto</codeph>, <codeph>verso</codeph>, <codeph>column</codeph> or <codeph>avoid-column</codeph></entry>
                            <entry><codeph>auto</codeph></entry>
                            <entry><xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-break-4/#break-between" scope="external" format="html">CSS Fragmentation 4 §3.1</xref></entry>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <entry><codeph>break-after</codeph></entry>
                            <entry>Forces or avoids a break after a block, a row or a row group, with the same values as <codeph>break-before</codeph>.</entry>
                            <entry>As <codeph>break-before</codeph></entry>
                            <entry><codeph>auto</codeph></entry>
                            <entry><xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-break-4/#break-between" scope="external" format="html">CSS Fragmentation 4 §3.1</xref></entry>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <entry><codeph>break-inside</codeph></entry>
                            <entry>Avoids a break inside a box, so that it stays on one page when it fits on one. A table header or footer group with <codeph>avoid</codeph> repeats on each page of the table.</entry>
                            <entry><codeph>auto</codeph>, <codeph>avoid</codeph>, <codeph>avoid-page</codeph> or <codeph>avoid-column</codeph></entry>
                            <entry><codeph>auto</codeph></entry>
                            <entry><xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-break-4/#break-within" scope="external" format="html">CSS Fragmentation 4 §3.2</xref></entry>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <entry><codeph>orphans</codeph></entry>
                            <entry>Sets how many lines of a paragraph must stay at the bottom of a page. If fewer fit, the whole paragraph goes to the next page.</entry>
                            <entry>An integer of 1 or more</entry>
                            <entry><codeph>2</codeph></entry>
                            <entry><xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-break-4/#widows-orphans" scope="external" format="html">CSS Fragmentation 4 §3.3</xref></entry>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <entry><codeph>widows</codeph></entry>
                            <entry>Sets how many lines of a paragraph must go to the top of the next page. If fewer would, lines from the previous page go with them.</entry>
                            <entry>An integer of 1 or more</entry>
                            <entry><codeph>2</codeph></entry>
                            <entry><xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-break-4/#widows-orphans" scope="external" format="html">CSS Fragmentation 4 §3.3</xref></entry>
                        </row>
                    </tbody>
                </tgroup>
            </table>
        </section>
        <section id="declarations-in-page-margin-rules">
            <title>Declarations in page-margin rules</title>
            <p>Each page-margin at-rule contains declarations written as <codeph>property: value;</codeph>. Use properties that apply to page-margin boxes, including <codeph>content</codeph>, font and text properties, color, backgrounds, borders, margins, padding, dimensions and <codeph>vertical-align</codeph>. See the <xref href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-page-3/#margin-property-list" scope="external" format="html">CSS Paged Media page-margin property list</xref>.</p>
            <p>For example, set a running title in the top-center box and a page number in the bottom-center box:</p>
            <pre outputclass="language-css21">@page {
    @top-center {
        content: "Annual report";
        font-weight: bold;
    }

    @bottom-center {
        content: "Page " counter(page);
        text-align: center;
    }
}
</pre>
        </section>
    </refbody>
</reference>

